{"book":23,"chapter":18,"context":{"chapter":18,"title":"Envoys From Beyond Cush","summary":"Isaiah addresses a tall, powerful nation beyond the rivers of Cush that sends envoys in papyrus boats. God will wait calmly, then prune the invader before harvest, and that distant people will bring gifts to Mount Zion.","background":"Cush (KJV 'Ethiopia') was the land south of Egypt along the upper Nile, roughly modern Sudan. In Isaiah's time a Cushite dynasty ruled Egypt, and its envoys sought allies against Assyria. Isaiah's answer: the world should watch for God's signal instead (v. 3).","customs":[{"term":"Vessels of bulrushes","verses":"18:2","note":"Light boats of bundled papyrus reeds, common on the Nile. Moses' 'ark of bulrushes' was made the same way (Exodus 2:3)."}],"watchFor":["God waits as quietly as summer heat and dew (v. 4).","The pruning comes just before the harvest (v. 5).","The feared nation ends up bringing gifts to Zion (v. 7)."],"connections":["Exodus 2:3","Zephaniah 3:10","Psalms 68:31","Acts 8:27"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["הוֹי","ho","H1945","HTj","alas!"],["אֶרֶץ","'eretz","H776","HNcfsc","O land of"],["צִלְצַל","tziltzal","H6767","HNcmsc","whirring of"],["כְּנָפָיִם","kenafayim","H3671","HNcfda","wings"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","which"],["מֵעֵבֶר","me'ever","H5676","HR/Ncmsa","[is] from [the] other side"],["לְנַהֲרֵי","lenaharei-","H5104","HR/Ncmpc","of [the] rivers of"],["כוּשׁ","khush","H3568","HNpl","Cush"]],"x":[[36003010,36003010,8],[12019009,12019009,6],[26030004,26030005,5],[36002012,36002012,5],[19063007,19063007,4],[8002012,8002012,3],[19017008,19017008,3],[19036007,19036007,3],[19057001,19057001,3],[19061004,19061004,3]],"xn":16},"2":{"w":[["הַשֹּׁלֵחַ","hasholeach","H7971","HTd/Vqrmsa","which sends"],["בַּיָּם","baiyam","H3220","HRd/Ncmsa","on the sea"],["צִירִים","tzirim","H6735","HNcmpa","envoys"],["וּבִכְלֵי","uvikhlei-","H3627","HC/R/Ncmpc","and in vessels of"],["גֹמֶא","gome'","H1573","HNcmsa","papyrus"],["עַל","'al-","H5921",